  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Calculate \n$\\int (5-8{cos}^{2}\u20612x)\\text{d}x.$",
  "worked_solution": "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u20612\\theta =2{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}\u20612\\theta +1).\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =2x$, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}\u20612x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}\u20614x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (5-8{cos}^{2}\u20612x)\\text{d}x & =\\int [5-8\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}\u20614x+1)]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int [5-4(\\operatorname{cos}\u20614x+1)]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (1-4\\operatorname{cos}\u20614x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x-4(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}\u20614x)+C \\\\  & =x-\\operatorname{sin}\u20614x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
